Spiking Neural Network adversarial robustness checking using PGD and FGSM (adapted for spiking) attacks. Uses Class Activation Maps and Saliency mapping
for explainable-AI techniques to understand model degradation under adv. perturbations.


Features

- **PGD & FGSM for Spiking Models**  
  Implements Projected Gradient Descent (PGD) and Fast Gradient Sign Method (FGSM) attacks, modified to account for discrete spike trains and membrane dynamics.

- **Explainable AI Techniques**  
  - **Class Activation Maps (CAMs)** to localize important spatial features.  
  - **Saliency Mapping** to highlight time-step contributions and neuron sensitivities.

- **Leaky Integrate-and-Fire (LIF) Backbone**  
  - BPTT with surrogate gradients for backpropagation through spike events.  
  - Configurable membrane time constants and thresholding behavior.

- **Modular & Extensible**  
  Easily swap in different SNN architectures, surrogate gradient functions, and attack parameters.

